# One SCA scanner, not four. grype, trivy and bearer each bring their own vulnerability database and
# their own walk of the tree, over the same pnpm lockfile that osv-scanner — which stays on, and
# reports nothing today — already covers. A project that needs container or SBOM scanning enables
# the one that answers that question, in its own config, rather than paying for three in CI.
**/*: grype, trivy, bearer

# Generated layer→subtree maps (devtools dockerfile --emit-oci-map): raw
# generator output must stay byte-stable for the Dockerfile drift gate.
docker/oci-map*.json: *
